  "text": "I'll independently review harnessloop commit `da8109c`: inspect the diff, hunt for author-missed defects, and write a review-only deliverable.Pulling the full implementation diff and checking version consistency plus edge cases in the fence parser.Checking version consistency, other parsers that may still lack fence guards, and CommonMark edge cases.Probing the unfixed E4 parser and residual false-green paths more carefully.Re-checking the E4 attack fixture — the earlier control was flawed — and waiting for validate.Restoring the harnessloop submodule after the detached checkout used for validation.## Summary\n\nAdversarial review of harnessloop **`da8109c`** (v0.29.0): fenced-code filtering via `_uncoded_lines` / `FENCE_MARKER_RE` for `parse_feedback`, `parse_review_fields`, and `parse_acceptance_eval_declaration`. The stated RAE flagship false-green is fixed; CommonMark fence rules and G27a–g bidirectional teeth are strong; `HARNESSLOOP_SKIP_CLAUDE=1 python3 scripts/validate.py` at this commit exits 0. The author’s own meta-lesson (“same bug in a new place”) is **not fully applied**: E4’s inline `- Verdict:` / `- Residuals:` scan in the same `verify_round` still uses raw `splitlines()` and is defeated by the same three-line fence pattern (false green and false red demonstrated). Version bump also left `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` at **0.11.0**.\n\n## Files touched\n\nnone (review only)\n\n## Acceptance verification (5/5 probes)\n\nMethod: `git show da8109c`; load `verify_protocol.py` blob into a temp module; tempfile fixtures matching G27’s `_rae_project` shape; ran full `scripts/validate.py` at `da8109c`. No tree edits retained (submodule restored to `main` / `c9c884e` after the checkout used for validation).\n\n| # | Probe | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Flagship RAE fence false-green closed | **OK** | Fenced `- Feedback: negative` + real `- Feedback: positive` → `parse_feedback == \"positive\"`; G27a full-project path fires `acceptance-eval-positive-without-pass` with failing ledger |\n| 2 | Fence state machine (type/length/info/indent/unclosed) | **OK** | G27b–f all green under validate; independent unit probes for info-string open, trailing-space close, cross-type non-close, 4-open/3-inner, unclosed→`None` |\n| 3 | Family sweep of all decision.md first-wins label parsers | **HIT (P0 residual)** | Finding 1 — E4 still unfenced |\n| 4 | Version manifests consistent at claimed 0.29.0 | **HIT (process)** | Finding 2 — codex plugin.json stuck at 0.11.0 |\n| 5 | Registered OUT honesty (4-space indented code) | **Documented residual** | G27e pins 4-space fence-shaped lines as *not* fences; still first-wins live prose (Finding 3) |\n\n### Finding 1 — P0 residual: E4 still raw first-wins (same class as the fix)\n\n**Location (at `da8109c`):** `verify_protocol.py` E4 block ~L3454–3465 — still:\n\n```python\nfor line in decision.read_text(...).splitlines():\n    ...\n    if ... startswith(\"- verdict:\"):\n    elif ... startswith(\"- residuals:\"):\n```\n\nThree named `parse_*` helpers route through `_uncoded_lines`; E4 does not. Comments even call E4 “the same narrow convention as `parse_review_fields`”.\n\n**False green** (should be `verdict-residual-contradiction`, kinds empty):\n\n```markdown\n# Decision\n\n```\n- Residuals: none\n```\n- Verdict: pass\n- Residuals: deferred migration still open\n- Review: none — n/a\n- Reviewer: me\n- Review verdict: pass\n```\n\nObserved: `kinds == []`. Raw fields: `('pass', 'none')`. Same text with `_uncoded_lines` applied: `('pass', 'deferred migration still open')` → would red.\n\n**False red** (real clean pass/none, fenced docs example poisons):\n\n```markdown\n```\n- Verdict: pass\n- Residuals: example residual for docs\n```\n- Verdict: pass\n- Residuals: none\n...\n```\n\nObserved: `verdict-residual-contradiction` present. Fixed path: no contradiction.\n\n**Why author missed it:** scoped “family” to three function names; grepped neither `startswith(\"- verdict: